Cheyenne Metropolitan Planning Organization (MPO)
Long-Range Metropolitan Transportation Plan (MTP)
Updated: September 30, 2024
Scope of Services
TASK 1. PROJECT MANAGEMENT
Task 1.1. Kick-Off Meeting
CONSULTANT will hold a virtual kick-off meeting with MPO staff to discuss the project scope of work,
schedule, data collection, public engagement elements, critical stakeholders, and project branding.
Task 1.2. Project Management Plan
CONSULTANT will develop a draft Project Management Plan (PMP). The PMP will include:
•
Key project staff, roles and responsibilities, staff resource plan, and contact information
•
Quality assurance/quality control (QA/QC) procedures for all deliverables
•
Final scope of work
•
Detailed milestone schedule
•
Branding suite that will include a plan logo with variations for different types of publications, a
comprehensive color palette to be used on all internal and public-facing deliverables, primary
and secondary fonts, as well as graphic elements and icons
•
Stakeholder Outreach Plan (SOP) that will include contact information for relevant
stakeholders, timeframes for stakeholder outreach efforts, and engagement methods.
•
Public Outreach Plan (POP) that will include virtual and in-person engagement methods,
timelines, staffing, and advertisement methods.
CONSULTANT will submit draft PMP to MPO staff for review.
CONSULTANT will finalize the PMP based on comments and direction from the MPO project
manager (PM).
Task 1.3. Invoicing and Ongoing Coordination
CONSULTANT will submit monthly invoices to the MPO with a brief progress report that summarizes
work competed during the month and work expected to be completed during the upcoming month.
Invoices will provide a task breakdown with hours expended by individual.
CONSULTANT will hold monthly virtual check-in meetings to facilitate continuous communication
between the CONSULTANT, and MPO, City of Cheyenne, and Laramie County staff.
Task 1 Deliverables
•
Kickoff meeting preparation, facilitation, and summary notes
•
Draft and final PMP document
Exhibit A
