TASK 2. PUBLIC AND STAKEHOLDER PARTICIPATION
The MPO desires to use a variety of outreach methodologies to ensure a range of opportunities for
residents, businesses, and property owners to participate in the MTP Update. Kimley-Horn’s public
participation plan will utilize a variety of techniques to gather input, respond to comments and
concerns, and keep decision makers informed at key project milestones. All materials for public
engagement will be developed in both English and Spanish.
Task 2.1. Project Website
CONSULTANT will work with the MPO to create website content for use in a project-specific
webpage in the MPO’s existing website. This website will house documentation created during the
project and will be made available to the public online. CONSULTANT will provide content copy,
graphics, documents, and links to external public engagement platforms.
Task 2.2. Public Engagement – Round 1
CONSULTANT will prepare for and conduct public and stakeholder engagement, which will include a
variety of in-person and virtual engagement strategies, with three emphases:
1.
Prioritize the goals to inform the recommendation prioritization process
2.
Provide the draft capital improvement projects for each mode of travel
3.
Obtain feedback and comments on the potential priority
CONSULTANT will create a web map that will allow the public to explore and review the proposed
projects and provide comments or upvotes. The web map will be developed using PublicCoordinate
and will be linked from the project-specific page on the MPO website.
CONSULTANT will collaborate with MPO staff to identify up to two pop-up locations/piggyback events
or one public open house to provide opportunities for the public to comment in person and to direct
them to virtual engagement options.
Task 2.3. Public Engagement – Round 2
CONSULTANT will prepare for and conduct a second round of public engagement, which will include
a variety of virtual engagement strategies, with two emphases:
1.
Informing the public that the draft MTP document is available for review and how to provide
comments
2.
Promote the high-priority projects and steps required to implement these projects after project
completion
CONSULTANT will create content to update the project website with the draft MTP document and an
opportunity for the public to provide comments on the draft document.
Exhibit A
