kimley-horn.com
6200 S Syracuse Way, Suite 300, Greenwood Village, CO 80111
303 228 2300
Task 3.3. MTP and Future Land Use Map Development
CONSULTANT will work with City of Cheyenne GIS staff to update the MTP map created for Connect
2045 to reflect the expanded MPO boundaries, existing and future roadway functional classifications,
and future land uses. CONSULTANT will rely on Cheyenne GIS staff to define the future land uses.
Task 3.4. Travel Demand Modeling
CONSULTANT will review the calibration of the updated regional travel demand model (TDM) and
adjust as necessary to ensure the model is meeting Federal Highway Administration guidance for
TDM calibration.
CONSULTANT will conduct up to five future year scenario model runs. Loaded network information
will be delivered to the MPO in both TransCAD and Esri GIS database format. CONSULTANT will
also provide PDF outputs showing volumes, link volume-to-capacity ratios, and other data outputs the
model may produce as directed by the MPO.
CONSULTANT will provide updated model documentation at the completion of the project detailing
the model file structure, model inputs and model outputs. Details of model validation will be included
as part of the documentation.
Task 3.5. Existing Conditions Assessment
CONSULTANT will conduct an update of the existing conditions analysis in Connect 2045 to
understand initiatives completed to date and evaluate the previous recommendations against
anticipated future development. Existing conditions analyses will be updated for:
•
Roadways and traffic performance
•
Transit
•
Greenways and on-street bicycle infrastructure
•
Sidewalks
•
Transportation safety
Task 3.6. Vision, Guiding Principal Review, and Evaluation Criteria
CONSULTANT will support the MPO in working with agency partners and the community to update
the goals, objectives, and evaluation criteria of Connect 2045 and ensure they are compliant with
State and Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act (IIJA) requirements. CONSULTANT will start this
effort by developing an MTP checklist that correlates the elements of the plan’s development with the
current state and federal requirements.
Based on the update goals and objectives, CONSULTANT will identify a set of key evaluation criteria
to use in prioritizing projects. Performance measures will be designed to reflect broadly held values in
the study area. CONSULTANT will develop a table that ties these elements together in a visual and
easily understandable manner, reinforcing that the established goals, objectives, and measures must
be considered together so their meaning and relationship are not lost. Where possible, Kimley-Horn
will equate evaluation criteria and targets in the MTP with system performance recorded in previous
reports to understand progress to date.
Exhibit A
