TASK 4. ALTERNATIVES DEVELOPMENT
CONSULTANT will compile findings from Task 3 to develop a range of multimodal improvements.
CONSULTANT anticipates this will include a confirmation of projects identified in Connect 2045
supplemented by new projects identified through the update process. Projects will be defined
sufficiently for the public and partner agencies to understand the general scale and scope and to
assess planning-level impacts and costs. CONSULTANT will conclude this task with updates to the
MTP project list and maps of the recommended transportation improvements. A statement of scope,
lead agency, anticipated year or timeframe for implementation, concept-level cost estimates in base
year and potential year of expenditure dollars, project type, funding source, and functional
classification (when applicable) for each project.
Task 4.1. Roadway System Recommendations
CONSULTANT will produce roadway strategies and recommendations across the MPO planning area
based upon future traffic and multimodal needs. CONSULTANT will incorporate complete streets
principals into all recommended projects for the roadway system. CONSULTANT will identify potential
costs and possible funding sources to implement each recommended improvement.
Task 4.2. Transit System Recommendations
CONSULTANT will produce transit strategies and recommendations for enhancing transit services
within the MPO’s planning area based upon forecasted future needs. Kimley-Horn will also identify
potential costs and possible funding sources to implement each recommended improvement.
Task 4.3. Regional Transit Recommendations
CONSULTANT will incorporate recommendations from past planning efforts surrounding Front Range
Passenger Rail and the ongoing MPO Passenger Rail Site Selection Study into the recommendations
list along with previously developed costs.
Task 4.4. Bikeways and Trails Network Recommendations
CONSULTANT will develop a recommended system that will be derived from several distinct parallel
tasks including:
•
Existing Plan Review
•
Public comment through public involvement activities
