roadway and traffic characteristics for potential crossings and intersection treatments. The proposed
system will be presented graphically on maps and in tables detailing distance, end points and other
key information.
Task 4.5. Safety Recommendations
CONSULTANT will outline safety objectives for the region and make recommendations to update
safety performance measures and management strategies outlined in Connect 2045 and the
upcoming Safe Streets and Roads for All (SS4A) funded Safety Action Plan for which the MPO has
been awarded federal funding, if available.
Task 4.6. Freight Recommendations
CONSULTANT will build upon the MPO’s 2017 Transportation Safety Management Plan and Connect
2045 to assess regional safety policies and programs. CONSULTANT also will utilize crash data
generated by the MPO to identify recommendations which address freight safety and help support
economic development of the metropolitan region.
Task 4.7. Travel and Tourism Recommendations
CONSULTANT will develop transportation recommendations that support the region’s tourist industry,
including festivals and casinos.
Task 4.8. Air Quality and Climate Change Considerations
CONSULTANT will incorporate air quality and climate change considerations as part of the
transportation planning process. CONSULTANT will provide strategies to manage and reduce
emissions from the transportation sector through identifying improvements to system operational
efficiencies, providing options for more energy-efficient modes and reduce growth of vehicle miles
traveled (VMT) as well as suggest alternatives and recommendations on preventing future congestion
and to develop goals and strategies of reducing VMT.
Task 4.9. System Resiliency and Reliability
CONSULTANT will identify strategies which reduce the vulnerability of existing transportation
infrastructure to natural disasters and prioritize suggestions that are unique to the MPO including:
exploring storm water facilities in accommodating flooding as well as assessing WYDOT intelligent
transportation systems which better communicate high wind and blizzard advisories to the freight
industry to more efficiently manage truck storage within the region.
Exhibit A
```

