Task 4.10. Emerging Technology Considerations
CONSULTANT will outline federal, state and municipal best practices assessment of policies
preparing for autonomous vehicles, emerging micro-mobility technologies, electric vehicle charging,
and present potential initial actions the MPO should consider in developing the MTP.
Task 4.11. Unincorporated Pockets Transportation Assessment
CONSULTANT will examine several existing unincorporated Laramie County pockets within the city
limits of Cheyenne and provide recommendations on how to best resolve transportation network
issues within those pocket areas created by the expected growth over the next 25 years.
Task 4.12. Ordinance Modifications
CONSULTANT will review and City of Cheyenne’s land development regulations and WYDOT’s
policies and procedures and identify potential modifications that may facilitating the MTP’s
implementation.
Task 4.13. Working Paper 2 – Alternatives Development
CONSULTANT will document the process and results of Task 4 activities in a draft working paper,
which will be submitted to MPO staff for review. CONSULTANT will finalize Working Paper 2 based
on MPO comments.
Task 4 Deliverables
•
Modal and policy recommendations lists
•
Draft and final Working Paper 2: Alternatives Development
TASK 5. PERFORMANCE BASED PLANNING
Using the project prioritization framework and the range of alternatives matrix, CONSULTANT will
support the MPO, its partners, and the public in prioritizing the list of identified transportation projects.
Task 5.1. Performance Based Prioritization
CONSULTANT will prioritize projects which most strongly support the locally identified MTP goals,
objectives and evaluation criteria. CONSULTANT will update the project prioritization spreadsheet
tool developed for Connect 2045 to the updated evaluation criteria and project list. CONSULTANT will
combine the technical prioritization, stakeholder and community engagement, and capital and
operating financial analysis into the final prioritized list of projects and implementation plan.
Task 5.2. Working Paper 3 – Alternative Prioritization
CONSULTANT will document the process and results of Task 5 activities in a draft working paper,
which will be submitted to MPO staff for review. CONSULTANT will finalize Working Paper 3 based
on MPO comments.
Task 5 Deliverables
•
Updated project prioritization spreadsheet tool
•
Draft and final Working Paper 2: Alternative Prioritization
Exhibit A
