TASK 6. FUDNING AND IMPLEMENTATION
CONSULTANT will develop Financial Plan that forecasts capital, operating, and maintenance
revenues and expenses.
Task 6.1. Cost Estimates
CONSULTANT will forecast available transportation capital funding and operating by 5-year
increments for the 2025-2050 time-period based on current sources and levels as input to
establishing the fiscally constrained plan.
Task 6.2. Funding Sources and Revenues
CONSULTANT will identify and evaluate funding and financing strategies that can be used for
generating additional funds needed for specific projects in the MTP and/or for expanding the available
funding for the fiscally constrained transportation plan.
Task 6.3. Action Plan
CONSULTANT will generate an action plan which documents how the MTP recommendations will be
implemented. This task will involves integrating a variety of factors associated with the identified
goals, objectives, and performance measures into a prioritization methodology in five-year increments
that are financially constrained within the 2050 planning horizon.
Task 6.4. Working Paper 4 – Implementation Plan
CONSULANT will document the process and results of Task 6 activities in a draft working paper
which will be submitted to MPO staff for review. CONSULTANT will finalize Working Paper 5 based
on MPO comments.
Task 6 Deliverables
•
Fiscal constraint tool
•
Draft and final Working Paper 4: Implementation Plan
TASK 7. DOCUMENTATION AND ADOPTION
Task 7.1. Draft and Final MTP
CONSULTANT will assemble the preceding work/tasks efforts into the MTP document. The resulting
draft and final plans will be easy to read and set forth an understandable transportation strategy for
the Cheyenne MPO region. At the completion of the project, CONSULTANT will transfer all GIS data
developed as part of the MTP update process and other data as requested by the MPO.
Task 7.2. Adoption Coordination
CONSULTANT will coordinate the MTP adoption process and requirements with MPO staff as laid
out in Task 2.
Task 7 Deliverables
•
Draft and final MTP document in an editable and PDF format
•
GIS and other datasets created during the MTP update
Exhibit A
